## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzles
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-03-01
Number: 11
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a shaded cross in the centre printed "No 11" (shown as _), under the heading "FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLES" and the words "Can You Solve Them?" drawn beside the grid. The number is printed only in the centre block. No credit line is printed. The key prints WELD for 19-20 ("To declare in card playing"), so 11-19 ("A don") reads DOW; the W is probably a turned M (MELD, DOM), but the grid follows the key as printed. Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_01_82.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_03_08_85.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


